The dance class consists of 20 students. Initially, 20% of the students are enrolled in contemporary dance. This is calculated as:

$$
20\% \text{ of } 20 = 0.20 \times 20 = 4 \text{ students}
$$

After accounting for the 4 students in contemporary dance, the remaining number of students is:

$$
20 - 4 = 16 \text{ students}
$$

Next, 25% of these remaining 16 students are enrolled in jazz dance. This is:

$$
25\% \text{ of } 16 = 0.25 \times 16 = 4 \text{ students}
$$

Thus, the remaining students who are enrolled in hip-hop dance are:

$$
16 - 4 = 12 \text{ students}
$$

To find the percentage of the entire class that is enrolled in hip-hop, we calculate:

$$
\frac{12}{20} \times 100 = 60\%
$$

This can also be verified using percentages directly:
- 20% in contemporary, 25% of the remaining 80% (20% of the total) in jazz, which is 20% of the total, leaving 60% for hip-hop.

