 The given problem is asking how much Cynthia will spend on ice cream after 60 days. She eats one serving of ice cream every night. Each carton contains 15 servings and costs $4.00. 

To solve this, first, we can calculate the total number of servings she will consume in 60 days. Since she eats one serving each night, she will eat 60 servings in 60 days.

Next, we need to determine how many cartons of ice cream she will need to buy. If each carton contains 15 servings, then the number of cartons she needs is 60 servings divided by 15 servings per carton. This calculation gives us the number of cartons she will have to buy in order to have enough servings for 60 days.

Finally, we need to find the total cost of these cartons. If each carton costs $4.00, then we can multiply the number of cartons by the price of each carton to find the total cost. 

