 The problem is asking how many bags of dog food Cecilia will use in the first year. 

First, we need to find out how much dog food the puppy will need in the first year. 

The first 180 days, the puppy needs 1 cup of dog food per day. So, for these days, the puppy will need: 180 days * 1 cup/day = 180 cups.

Then, for the rest of the year, the puppy needs 2 cups of dog food per day. There are 365 days in a year, so the rest of the year is 365 days - 180 days = 185 days.

For these 185 days, the puppy will need: 185 days * 2 cups/day = 370 cups.

Now, adding the two amounts together, the total cups of dog food needed in the first year is: 180 cups + 370 cups = 550 cups.

Since one bag of dog food contains 110 cups, we need to divide the total cups needed by the number of cups per bag: 550 cups ÷ 110 cups/bag = 5 bags.

